  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R3-013$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A project handoff is delayed because everyone thought someone else would send the file. The next stage depends on several people understanding their ownership. What is the best improvement?$qb$, $qb$Agree one named owner and a clear handoff time for the next cycle$qb$, $qb$Add the handoff to the team checklist$qb$, $qb$Ask everyone to remember the file next time$qb$, $qb$Ask the manager to send the file in future$qb$, $qb$Let the receiving team chase the file$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R3-014$qb$, $qb$A1-08$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A simple trial of a new method saves time with no quality loss. The improvement may later be used by other team members. What should you do next?$qb$, $qb$Document the result and propose a controlled wider trial$qb$, $qb$Repeat the method on a few similar tasks$qb$, $qb$Replace the old method immediately for all work$qb$, $qb$Keep using it only for your own tasks$qb$, $qb$Return to the old method because it is approved$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R3-015$qb$, $qb$A1-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague criticizes your idea and you feel an urge to interrupt. You still need to contribute constructively to the rest of the meeting. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Let them finish, notice your reaction, and answer the substance of the criticism$qb$, $qb$Listen fully and ask one question before replying$qb$, $qb$Interrupt briefly to correct a factual point$qb$, $qb$Stay silent even when it is your turn to respond$qb$, $qb$Interrupt so your idea is not misunderstood$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R3-016$qb$, $qb$A1-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$An AI tool gives two different answers to the same factual question. The output may be used in a customer-facing decision. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Check the fact using a reliable independent source before using either answer$qb$, $qb$Compare the two answers and identify where they differ$qb$, $qb$Ask the AI a third time and use the majority answer$qb$, $qb$Choose the answer that sounds more detailed$qb$, $qb$Use the first answer because it came first$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R3-037$qb$, $qb$A1-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A new approved system now performs a calculation you used to do manually. The old method still feels easier because you have more practice with it. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Verify the new calculation during transition, then stop the manual duplicate once confidence is established$qb$, $qb$Compare the new result with your manual calculation for a short period$qb$, $qb$Keep doing both calculations permanently$qb$, $qb$Trust only the manual calculation for important work$qb$, $qb$Avoid the new system$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
