  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R4-015$qb$, $qb$A1-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A difficult stakeholder meeting leaves you frustrated, but you must make an important decision immediately afterward. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Create a brief pause, separate the emotional reaction from the decision facts, and check whether your judgement is being affected$qb$, $qb$Take a short break and review the key facts before deciding$qb$, $qb$Make the decision quickly while the meeting details are fresh$qb$, $qb$Delay every decision until the next day$qb$, $qb$Ask someone else to decide because you are frustrated$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R4-016$qb$, $qb$A1-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$An AI tool recommends a customer action based on historical data, but current market conditions have changed. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Reassess the recommendation using current evidence, test whether the historical pattern still applies, and own the final judgement$qb$, $qb$Add current market information and review how it changes the recommendation$qb$, $qb$Use the AI result because historical data is more objective$qb$, $qb$Reject the AI result because conditions changed$qb$, $qb$Present the AI recommendation without taking a position$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R4-037$qb$, $qb$A1-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A standardized process replaces a personal method that produced good individual results but made team handoffs inconsistent. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Adopt the common process, understand the collaboration benefit, and propose evidence-based improvements through the shared process rather than keeping a private variation$qb$, $qb$Use the standard process while comparing outcomes during transition$qb$, $qb$Keep the personal method for work you handle alone$qb$, $qb$Use whichever method is faster$qb$, $qb$Continue the personal method until someone explicitly stops it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R6-011$qb$, $qb$A1-09$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A new work rule is introduced with little notice. The team must keep delivering while the change is being learned. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Understand the required change, apply it, and quickly clarify anything that could affect your work$qb$, $qb$Read the rule and ask focused questions where needed$qb$, $qb$Wait for teammates to show how they interpret it$qb$, $qb$Continue the old way until a manager checks$qb$, $qb$Ignore the rule because notice was short$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R6-012$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager asks for an update and you have good progress but also one new risk. Both priorities have legitimate consequences and cannot simply be ignored. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Share the progress, explain the risk and impact, and state what decision or help is needed$qb$, $qb$Give the progress and flag the new risk clearly$qb$, $qb$Focus on the progress and mention the risk later$qb$, $qb$Report only the risk so it gets attention$qb$, $qb$Say everything is on track$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R6-013$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A teammate completes their part, but another person does not know the handoff is ready. Several people depend on the handoff being coordinated correctly. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Make the handoff visible to the next owner and confirm the next action$qb$, $qb$Notify the next person that the work is ready$qb$, $qb$Assume they will see the status in the system$qb$, $qb$Tell the manager the first part is complete$qb$, $qb$Wait until the next person asks$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
