  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R6-015$qb$, $qb$A1-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A teammate's comment irritates you during a meeting, but the discussion must continue. You need to make a fair decision without carrying the emotion into it. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Notice the reaction, stay with the issue, and respond to the facts rather than the irritation$qb$, $qb$Pause before replying and ask what the teammate means$qb$, $qb$Hide the irritation but keep arguing your point$qb$, $qb$Tell the teammate their comment was irritating$qb$, $qb$Leave the meeting$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
