  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R6-015$qb$, $qb$A1-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You receive a message that makes you angry just before a meeting. You must make another important judgement immediately afterward and cannot allow emotion to distort it. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Pause, settle your reaction, and respond after checking the facts$qb$, $qb$Take a short break before deciding whether a reply is needed$qb$, $qb$Reply briefly so the issue does not stay unresolved$qb$, $qb$Tell a coworker how unreasonable the message was$qb$, $qb$Send your first response while the issue is fresh$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R6-016$qb$, $qb$A1-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$An AI tool gives you a confident answer for a work task. The output may influence a material customer or management decision, so evidence quality matters. What should you do before using it?$qb$, $qb$Check the important facts against a reliable source$qb$, $qb$Review the answer for obvious errors and missing context$qb$, $qb$Use it if it matches what you expected$qb$, $qb$Ask the AI tool to confirm that its answer is correct$qb$, $qb$Copy it directly because the wording sounds confident$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R6-037$qb$, $qb$A1-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A new approved method replaces a shortcut you have used successfully for months. The old method remains personally effective but creates inconsistency across the wider operation. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Learn and test the new method before deciding it is worse$qb$, $qb$Use the new method for the next few tasks and compare results$qb$, $qb$Keep your shortcut for important work and use the new method elsewhere$qb$, $qb$Wait until most teammates stop using the old method$qb$, $qb$Ignore the change because your shortcut still works$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R6-038$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have enough information to start safely, but one minor detail is still unknown. The objective is stable, but important requirements will remain uncertain after work begins. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Start the safe work and review the detail when it becomes available$qb$, $qb$State your assumption and begin the parts that are unaffected$qb$, $qb$Wait until every detail is confirmed$qb$, $qb$Guess the missing detail and complete everything$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager to take responsibility for the uncertainty$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R6-039$qb$, $qb$A1-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$AI creates a useful first draft, but it misses important customer context. The AI contribution is useful, but current context includes information absent from its data. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Add the missing context, verify key facts, and take responsibility for the final version$qb$, $qb$Edit the draft using your knowledge of the customer$qb$, $qb$Ask the AI to rewrite it with more detail$qb$, $qb$Send the draft to a colleague without reviewing it$qb$, $qb$Use the draft unchanged because AI created it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R7-011$qb$, $qb$A1-09$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A software update changes the screen you use every day. The team must maintain performance while the new method becomes standard. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Learn the new layout and practice the changed steps$qb$, $qb$Read the update notes and try the new screen$qb$, $qb$Keep using an old shortcut until it stops working$qb$, $qb$Ask a teammate to do the changed steps for you$qb$, $qb$Complain about the update and avoid using it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R7-012$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You finish a task differently from what your manager expected, although the result is correct. You own the result, but competing senior expectations must be reconciled. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Explain your approach and check the preferred method for future work$qb$, $qb$Show the result and ask whether the approach is acceptable$qb$, $qb$Keep using your method because the result is correct$qb$, $qb$Change the work without discussing why$qb$, $qb$Avoid mentioning the difference$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
