  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R1-014$qb$, $qb$A1-08$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A manual check catches almost no issues but takes significant time. The pilot is promising, but scale will change roles, controls, dependencies, and exception volumes. What is the best next step?$qb$, $qb$Review the risk the check is meant to control and test a more efficient way to manage it$qb$, $qb$Collect evidence on what the check has caught before suggesting a change$qb$, $qb$Stop the check because it rarely finds problems$qb$, $qb$Automate the check immediately without reviewing its purpose$qb$, $qb$Keep it unchanged because it is part of the process$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R1-015$qb$, $qb$A1-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are annoyed by repeated questions from a colleague during a busy period. The interaction is high stakes and could bias a decision with wider organizational consequences. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Notice your frustration, answer respectfully, and agree a better way to group future questions$qb$, $qb$Answer the current question and suggest a set time for later questions$qb$, $qb$Give very short answers so the interruptions end faster$qb$, $qb$Tell them they ask too many questions$qb$, $qb$Stop responding$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
