  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R1-037$qb$, $qb$A1-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A new standard removes a step you were taught as essential. The old operating approach still produces strong local results but conflicts with the consistency required across the organization. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Understand why the standard changed, follow the current method, and stop the old step once confirmed$qb$, $qb$Compare the new standard with the old method and clarify any concern$qb$, $qb$Keep the old step as extra protection$qb$, $qb$Use the old method for important cases$qb$, $qb$Ignore the new standard$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
