  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R2-015$qb$, $qb$A1-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A teammate's comment irritates you during a meeting, but the discussion must continue. The interaction is high stakes and could distort a decision with wider organizational consequences. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Notice the reaction, stay with the issue, and respond to the facts rather than the irritation$qb$, $qb$Pause before replying and ask what the teammate means$qb$, $qb$Hide the irritation but keep arguing your point$qb$, $qb$Tell the teammate their comment was irritating$qb$, $qb$Leave the meeting$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R2-016$qb$, $qb$A1-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$An AI-generated answer includes a quotation that you cannot find in the source. The AI output may shape a material decision, but model assumptions and current business context are not fully aligned. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Remove or correct the quotation after checking the original source$qb$, $qb$Search the source and verify the quotation before using it$qb$, $qb$Use the quotation without quotation marks$qb$, $qb$Ask AI to confirm the quotation$qb$, $qb$Keep it because the rest of the answer is accurate$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R2-037$qb$, $qb$A1-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A new procedure removes a control you used for years because the control is now built into the system. The previous operating approach still produces strong local results but conflicts with consistency required across the organization. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Verify the system control works as intended, then stop duplicating the old manual control$qb$, $qb$Check the new control during transition and follow the updated procedure$qb$, $qb$Keep the manual control permanently$qb$, $qb$Use the old control only on important cases$qb$, $qb$Ignore the updated procedure$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R3-011$qb$, $qb$A1-09$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The change is mandatory across several teams, but local conditions make its impact uneven and performance cannot pause. Which approach demonstrates high adaptability during a department-wide migration to a new operational platform?$qb$, $qb$Proactively mastering key workflows, creating quick-reference guides for peers, and integrating the platform into daily habits.$qb$, $qb$Attending mandatory training sessions carefully and adjusting daily routines to meet official compliance mandates.$qb$, $qb$Maintaining personal offline tracking spreadsheets while gradually entering required data into the new platform.$qb$, $qb$Suggesting to supervisors that full platform migration be postponed until peak operational cycles pass.$qb$, $qb$Restricting tool usage strictly to mandatory fields while preserving legacy operational habits where possible.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R3-012$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have decision authority, while two senior stakeholders are pressing incompatible priorities and expect immediate action. What is the best course of action when a manager assigns an urgent task that conflicts with a previously set deadline?$qb$, $qb$Confirming priority expectations directly with the manager by presenting workload timelines and trade-offs.$qb$, $qb$Accepting the urgent task immediately and working extended hours to complete both deliverables on schedule.$qb$, $qb$Prioritizing the urgent task right away and notifying the manager about the original missed deadline after it occurs.$qb$, $qb$Asking a colleague to take over the original assignment so you can focus exclusively on the manager's new request.$qb$, $qb$Completing the original task first to honor the initial commitment before beginning the new priority assignment.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R3-013$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$All workstreams appear healthy individually, yet conflicting decisions are creating program-level rework and launch risk. How should an employee integrate effectively when joining a team with established informal working norms?$qb$, $qb$Observing team communication habits, respecting established norms, and building trust through reliable task delivery.$qb$, $qb$Proposing the adoption of successful communication templates from your previous department during early team meetings.$qb$, $qb$Focusing on delivering assigned tasks independently while participating politely during formal group discussions.$qb$, $qb$Scheduling check-in meetings with senior team members to seek advice on how to stand out within the group.$qb$, $qb$Maintaining your established personal working style, assuming individual deliverable quality is the sole performance driver.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R3-014$qb$, $qb$A1-08$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The pilot succeeded locally, but enterprise scale will change roles, exception volumes, controls, and support needs. What key action reflects agility when analytics reveal a ongoing operational campaign is underperforming metrics by 30%?$qb$, $qb$Reallocating resources toward high-performing channels based on data analysis and adjusting tactical milestones.$qb$, $qb$Increasing activity frequency on existing channels to offset underperformance through higher volume.$qb$, $qb$Maintaining the current campaign structure until the scheduled end date before conducting a post-mortem review.$qb$, $qb$Escalating underperformance metrics to leadership with a recommendation to halt campaign activities entirely.$qb$, $qb$Adjusting progress report targets downward to align stated benchmarks with actual performance figures.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R3-015$qb$, $qb$A1-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The challenge is personal and public, but the decision that follows has material organizational consequences. How does an employee display emotional presence when unexpected technical issues interrupt a live client presentation?$qb$, $qb$Preserving composure, acknowledging the interruption calmly, and transitioning smoothly to offline summary materials.$qb$, $qb$Apologizing repeatedly to stakeholders while attempting to resolve technical issues on screen.$qb$, $qb$Requesting a colleague to take over verbal presentation duties while you troubleshoot software issues.$qb$, $qb$Proposing a temporary meeting pause so participants can reconvene after technical issues are fixed.$qb$, $qb$Skipping remaining presentation slides to deliver a brief verbal summary and conclude the meeting quickly.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R3-016$qb$, $qb$A1-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The model result is influential, yet recent operating evidence conflicts with assumptions embedded in the analysis. What is the correct practice for integrating AI text summarization tools into executive reporting workflows?$qb$, $qb$Auditing AI-generated summaries against raw source data to verify accuracy before finalizing insights.$qb$, $qb$Copying AI-generated summaries directly into final reporting decks to maximize operational processing speed.$qb$, $qb$Analyzing all raw data manually as usual, using AI tools strictly as a secondary check after drafting reports.$qb$, $qb$Forwarding raw dataset files directly into AI tools and distributing generated summaries to leadership.$qb$, $qb$Avoiding AI analytical tools entirely until formal accuracy benchmarks are published by IT departments.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R3-037$qb$, $qb$A1-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$An approved new method replaces a familiar way of working. The old approach still produces excellent local results but prevents consistent handoffs and comparable performance across the organization. What response shows the best judgement?$qb$, $qb$Relinquishing outmoded working habits, actively mastering new frameworks, and supporting team adaptation.$qb$, $qb$Adopting new framework terminology during meetings while keeping familiar tracking methods in personal notes.$qb$, $qb$Requesting permission to use legacy frameworks for ongoing work while applying new frameworks to new tasks.$qb$, $qb$Attending training workshops and waiting for senior peers to demonstrate how new frameworks apply to daily work.$qb$, $qb$Comparing legacy framework benefits against new framework drawbacks during team discussions.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R3-038$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The strategic objective is clear, but evidence from pilots will continue changing important requirements during execution. What approach is most effective when coordinating a new project with fluid scope and evolving goals?$qb$, $qb$Anchoring execution around short-term operational milestones, setting feedback loops, and adapting dynamically.$qb$, $qb$Drafting a rigid project master timeline based on standard operational assumptions and seeking approval.$qb$, $qb$Pausing active project execution until leadership provides a fully defined, fixed scope document.$qb$, $qb$Focusing effort on routine administrative tasks while waiting for project scope clarity to develop.$qb$, $qb$Relying on senior team members to make primary project decisions until official guidelines are issued.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R3-039$qb$, $qb$A1-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The AI analysis is sophisticated and persuasive, but it lacks a current organizational constraint that could reverse the recommendation. How is human-AI synergy best achieved when utilizing AI tools for client document generation?$qb$, $qb$Contextualizing AI-generated drafts by auditing source data, adding industry insights, and refining tone.$qb$, $qb$Reviewing AI-generated text for basic grammar and formatting errors before client submission.$qb$, $qb$Using AI tools exclusively to generate outline headings, writing all draft text manually from scratch.$qb$, $qb$Submitting AI-generated document drafts directly to team leads for review without manual edits.$qb$, $qb$Avoiding AI generation tools for client deliverables due to general data privacy concerns.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R4-011$qb$, $qb$A1-09$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team starts using a new process that changes how you do a routine task. The change spans several teams with different operating realities, while service commitments must continue. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Learn the new steps and use them in your next task$qb$, $qb$Attend the training and ask questions where needed$qb$, $qb$Use both old and new methods until you feel confident$qb$, $qb$Wait to see how experienced teammates handle it$qb$, $qb$Keep using the old method because it is faster$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
