  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-25PLUS-R08-013$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your executive team has strong functional accountability but no one owns outcomes that span the full customer journey. What should you change?$qb$, $qb$Create end-to-end outcome ownership and cross-functional decision rights while preserving functional accountability for the capabilities each area contributes.$qb$, $qb$Take a credible immediate action on the visible issue and defer broader institutional implications to the next governance cycle.$qb$, $qb$Gather more evidence and make a limited adjustment without resolving the central enterprise trade-off.$qb$, $qb$Preserve the current framework and ask affected leaders to manage the consequences within their areas.$qb$, $qb$Maintain the existing course until external events make change unavoidable.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-25PLUS-R08-014$qb$, $qb$A1-08$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A new platform could make your product easier to distribute but also give the platform owner control over customer data and pricing. What is strongest?$qb$, $qb$Evaluate access benefits against future bargaining power and data control, test multiple channel positions, and preserve alternatives rather than optimizing only near-term distribution.$qb$, $qb$Apply the closest existing precedent with added safeguards, although it does not fully address the strategic context.$qb$, $qb$Escalate for a higher-level ruling before fully examining competing assumptions and consequences.$qb$, $qb$Choose the fastest workable compromise without addressing the underlying driver.$qb$, $qb$Protect the current target or position even if material risk is transferred elsewhere.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-25PLUS-R08-015$qb$, $qb$A1-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A board member makes a harsh criticism of a proposal you personally developed. You notice yourself preparing a rebuttal before they finish. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Slow your response, listen for the strongest substantive point, separate identity from the proposal, and answer the evidence rather than the emotional impact of the criticism.$qb$, $qb$Improve the current model incrementally while retaining its core incentives, assumptions and decision structure.$qb$, $qb$Seek additional stakeholder input but do not establish how contradictory evidence or interests will be resolved.$qb$, $qb$Make a unilateral short-term choice that reduces visible tension but leaves the systemic mechanism unchanged.$qb$, $qb$Avoid intervention because changing an established model could create additional uncertainty.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-25PLUS-R08-016$qb$, $qb$A1-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$An AI system predicts which communities will generate the highest return from branch closures, but it does not model access for vulnerable customers. What is strongest?$qb$, $qb$Add service-access and distributional consequences to the decision, test model assumptions, use accountable human judgment and ensure efficiency does not become the sole objective.$qb$, $qb$Address the largest immediate risk and defer less visible enterprise consequences until the next planning cycle.$qb$, $qb$Run a bounded pilot but leave success criteria and the next decision threshold undefined.$qb$, $qb$Ask relevant operating leaders to absorb the issue within existing authority and resources.$qb$, $qb$Choose the option that best protects current reported performance and reputation.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
